  <!-- ── About the book ────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section book-section">
    <div class="book-section-inner">
      <h2 class="section-heading">About the book</h2>
      <div class="book-prose">
        <p>
          <em>Vibe Coding</em> is a practical book about a new way of building
          software, where intent and conversational flow matter more than syntax.
          Developers describe what they want; the system builds it. The book
          lays out how to harness GenAI at production scale without losing the
          engineering excellence modern systems demand.
        </p>
        <p>
          The authors draw on decades of combined experience in software
          engineering and developer productivity — Gene from the DevOps
          and Phoenix Project arc, me from Amazon, Google, Grab, and
          Sourcegraph — to walk through how teams transform programming
          challenges into fluid conversations with coding agents while still
          shipping real systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          The book won the <strong>Gold Medal at the 2026 Axiom Book Awards</strong>
          and <strong>Silver at the 2026 IBPA Benjamin Franklin Awards</strong>
          in the Professional &amp; Technical category.
        </p>
        <p class="book-prose-meta">
          320 pages · paperback, ebook, audiobook · IT Revolution · October 2025
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

